{"type":"text","timestamp":1788480202776,"sessionID":"ses_f96499560ffeg5ToJAP0YiOCHb","part":{"id":"prt_069ba17a400142yUC5mPYXazNi","messageID":"msg_069ba0af70010i7cBFmVY9gzEE","sessionID":"ses_f96499560ffeg5ToJAP0YiOCHb","type":"text","text":"Done. Extended `dspy.Image` / `encode_image` (dspy/adapters/types/image.py) to support any file type, matching upstream DSPy PR #7872:\n\n- **`encode_image`** (dspy/adapters/types/image.py:81) now accepts any data URI (`data:` prefix, not just `data:image/`), so PDFs, videos, and other files pass through unchanged.\n- **`_encode_image_from_file`** (line 132) reads local files and detects MIME type via `mimetypes.guess_type`, raising a clear `ValueError` when it can't be determined.\n- **`_encode_image_from_url`** (line 146) uses the response's `Content-Type` header, falling back to URL-based MIME detection with a clear error if neither works.\n- **`_encode_pil_image`** (line 165) maps the PIL image format to its proper MIME type instead of assuming it.\n- **`is_image`** (line 187) now recognizes any data URI plus existing local paths/URLs/PIL images.\n\nAdded 4 tests (`test_pdf_url_support`, `test_different_mime_types`, `test_mime_type_from_response_headers`, `test_pdf_from_file`). All 52 signature tests and 8 adapter tests pass; `ruff check` is clean.","time":{"start":1788480198564,"end":1788480202774}}}
